    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0108" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">803.01/10–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Heath</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-04">October 4,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received October 4—12:57 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>833. <hi rendition="#italic">Otechestven Front</hi> today publishes text of
                    telegram to Chou En-lai, Minister Foreign Affairs Central People’s Government
                    Chinese People’s Republic, acknowledging receipt of communication of October 1
                    from latter government and stating Bulgarian Government will establish
                    diplomatic relations with People’s Republic China and exchange
                    representatives.</p>
                <p>Also publishes article reporting establishment diplomatic relations between USSR
                    and People’s Republic China and breaking relations with Canton.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Heath</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
